From efbc5b7df5bfa02f51a562ad185ca8d389d734ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Gre=C5=84?= <witold.gren@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:37:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rtsp: end a live view when the camera stops sending, and
 measure recordings by their frames

A camera that stopped sending after a few frames left the live view waiting forever for the
next one, and the waiting stream kept the camera's session open: a battery camera stayed
awake for 90 minutes, reconnecting every half hour, and the recorder kept a file of 0.4 s
named as 90 minutes. A live view now ends after 20 s without a frame (not when paused on
motion), and a recording's length and end come from its first and last frame.
